          "jsCode": "// One place to read what actually happened. Both platforms report success\n// differently \u2014 Instagram returns the published media id, Facebook Reels\n// returns {success:true} and the id came back in the start phase.\nconst v = $('Normalise Input').item.json;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  instagramMediaId: $('IG Publish').item.json.id ?? null,\n  facebookVideoId: $('FB Reel Start').item.json.video_id ?? null,\n  facebookFinished: $('FB Reel Finish').item.json.success === true,\n  caption: v.caption,\n  facebookCaption: v.facebookCaption,\n  durationSeconds: v.duration,\n  // Cosmetic and deliberately non-fatal: both cover nodes are\n  // continueRegularOutput, because they run *after* the Reel is\n  // already live on both platforms and must never fail a published run.\n  facebookCoverSet: $('FB Set Reel Cover').item.json?.id != null\n                 || $('FB Set Reel Cover').item.json?.success === true,\n} }];"
